Reconciled public HeartbeatData API surface against pinned remoting HeartbeatData.java. Java exposes computeHeartbeatFingerprint; Rust currently only has a private core helper. Added a protocol-level regression against actual Java fingerprints for all seven runtime cases. Focused compile-red exit101: no public compute_heartbeat_fingerprint method on HeartbeatData. Preparing separate public-API implementation; existing null collection cases constrain JSON-round-trip defaults.
Public heartbeat fingerprint implementation: added `HeartbeatData::compute_heartbeat_fingerprint() -> Result<i32, serde_json::Error>` in protocol and switched core fingerprint use to it. It preserves Java's JSON-copy null-collection defaults, normalized fields, subVersion reset, deterministic set order and UTF-16 String.hashCode. New public protocol API regression matches all seven invoked Java singleton cases. Full socket-enabled workspace all-target suite, strict all-feature/all-target Clippy, pinned Maven verify, fmt/diff and differential comparator/22-manifest pass. Preparing implementation commit and compatibility/API inventory docs; broader public API reconciliation remains open.
Public fingerprint API committed 3c4f444. Updated heartbeat/route/Phase6 requirement/general compatibility/API configuration inventories with the API mapping and current parity evidence. Pinned Java source remains read-only; other public API/source/input audit is still required.
Extended actual Java heartbeat runtime oracle for an owner whose `subscriptions()` returns null. Pinned `prepareHeartbeatData(false)` throws NullPointerException; simple preparation succeeds with empty subscription data. Fixture SHA-256 189e4a80c6f7f02083efc15dfe39535321872860a3d058c77eca975564193036. Existing Rust runtime behavior matches both assertions; focused regression and pinned Maven verify pass. Preparing standalone oracle/test/log commit, then updating heartbeat and requirement audit. Java checkout remains untouched.
