Registry custom-equality oracle/red: extended pinned Java 5.5.1 live producer/consumer ConcurrentMap fixtures with owner values whose `equals` matches by key. `replace(key, equivalent, new)` and `remove(key, equivalent)` all return true for both tables. Client-config fixture SHA-256 daeb2fde29ccf911064c779a40a5907645c61764f2d0de6960f13e9333a676fe. Native regression currently compile-fails because owner traits have no value equality mapping and ProducerTable/ConsumerTable expose only identity conditional methods. Preparing source-compatible equality capability while retaining identity-lease cleanup.
Registry equality implementation: owner traits provide an optional stable equality key captured before registry locks; `replace_if_equal/remove_if_equal` now match Java conditional ConcurrentMap value semantics. Explicit `replace_if_same/remove_if_same` preserve native Arc identity operations, and lifecycle lease cleanup remains identity-based. Both producer and consumer custom-equality oracle cases pass. Full socket-enabled workspace all-target suite, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, pinned Maven verify, formatter/diff and comparator/22-manifest pass. Fixture hash daeb2fde29ccf911064c779a40a5907645c61764f2d0de6960f13e9333a676fe. Preparing independent implementation commit, then ADR/API requirement updates; default map operations and broader source audit remain open.
Registry equality implementation committed b9f5bb6. Updated ADR-0009, API/config method map and P6-04 requirement row with verified custom equality behavior and the remaining stable-key/mutable-equality and default-operation boundaries. Whole Phase6 remains incomplete.
ConcurrentMap default-operation audit: pinned Java live producer/consumer tables invoke computeIfAbsent, computeIfPresent, compute, merge, replaceAll, forEach, keySet and values. Oracle records insertion/remapping/removal, callback counts, result key snapshots and counts; config fixture SHA-256 ca02053ee3d488fa6b907fff28557ae39da53ae4681829a0b6c4bc81e966bddd. Native regression compile-red exit101: ProducerTable/ConsumerTable lack compute, merge, iteration and key/value snapshot methods. Preparing Rust-native default-operation counterparts with retrying conditional updates.
Registry default map implementation: ProducerTable/ConsumerTable now expose retrying `compute_if_absent`, `compute_if_present`, `compute`, `merge`, and `replace_all`; detached `keys`, `values`, and `for_each` iteration snapshots. Conditional retries use the Java-value-equality methods; user closures run outside registry mutexes. Matching Java invocation regression passes for both tables, including compute/merge results, callback counts and snapshots. Full socket-enabled workspace all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, pinned Maven verify, fmt/diff and comparator/22-manifest pass. Preparing independent implementation commit then updating ADR/API mapping. Live mutable Java keySet/values view semantics remain a possible gap and must stay explicitly documented.
