Pinned Java 5.5.1 live-view fixture now invokes removeIf and retainAll through keySet, values and entrySet for both producer and consumer ConcurrentMaps. All six outcomes per map are true and confirm backing mappings are changed. Client-config fixture SHA-256 60212adf7edc40e92763d4df205a151bf6a1787afe4324bf41fd3edae7545c92; offline Maven verify passes. Preparing oracle-only commit before native bulk-view tests.
Added Rust integration assertions for Java removeIf/retainAll semantics through key-set, values and entry-set handles on both table types. Test is compile-red for missing remove_if/retain view methods (exit101). The pinned Java fixture confirms all six operations mutate the backing maps and has SHA-256 60212adf7edc40e92763d4df205a151bf6a1787afe4324bf41fd3edae7545c92. Preparing separate red-test commit.
Implemented closure-based bulk operations on live views: key-set, values and entry-set handles now expose `remove_if`/`retain`, evaluating predicates over detached snapshots and applying conditional/direct removals outside registry locks. Both producer and consumer tests pass against the six pinned Java removeIf/retainAll outcomes. Full socket-enabled workspace tests, strict Clippy, pinned Maven verify for fixture SHA-256 60212adf7edc40e92763d4df205a151bf6a1787afe4324bf41fd3edae7545c92, fmt/diff and comparator/manifest22 pass. Java iterator removal and exact collection-overload semantics remain open. Preparing implementation commit.
Updated ADR-0009, the API map and P6-04 audit for closure-based live-view `remove_if`/`retain`, supported by actual Java removeIf/retainAll fixture cases. Documentation now distinguishes these predicate mutations from Java iterator removal, weakly consistent iteration and exact Collection overloads, which remain under audit. Fixture SHA-256 60212adf7edc40e92763d4df205a151bf6a1787afe4324bf41fd3edae7545c92; full workspace tests, strict Clippy, pinned Maven, fmt/diff and comparator/manifest22 pass. Preparing separate docs commit.
Updated registry documentation to describe predicate-based `remove_if`/`retain`, their Java removeIf/retainAll oracle coverage, and their detached-snapshot concurrency boundary. Remaining work is Java iterator removal/weak iteration and exact collection-overload API, plus dynamic equality and broader source/input audit. Final fixture SHA-256 60212adf7edc40e92763d4df205a151bf6a1787afe4324bf41fd3edae7545c92; full workspace, strict Clippy, pinned Maven, fmt/diff, comparator and manifest22 pass. Preparing separate documentation commit.
