Added native regressions for collection-membership `remove_all`/`retain_all` on key, value and entry handles for both tables. Compile-red confirms the exact collection methods are absent (exit101). Java oracle fields for all six operations are true; current fixture SHA-256 43023d1528988060466a67ad87feab6c0c3c3fd0c9f656af1d13d935828a60f9. Preparing separate red-test commit.
Extended Java custom-equality fixtures for values-view removeAll/retainAll and entry-set retainAll on both map types. Equal-but-distinct owners are kept/removed exactly as ConcurrentHashMap Collection semantics require; six outcomes all pass. Fixture SHA-256 fc7119b073dbd6e6da0d1219352f7cc91606ad3df11ff3fc7a8e6eced759ec4c; pinned Maven verify passes. Preparing oracle-only commit.
Native tests now compare custom-equality removeAll/retainAll results against the latest Java fixture for producer/consumer value and entry views. Both focused equality and basic/bulk view regressions pass. The initial local equality assertion exposed that its moved `producer_other/consumer_other` Arcs expired under the intended weak-owner contract; retaining each owner fixed the test setup. Preparing separate native test commit; implementation remains in progress.
Implemented collection-membership methods on retained views: key views accept BTreeSet keys; values views accept owner slices and compare each candidate using the mapping's captured Java equality; entry views accept a key/value map and compare key plus Java value equality. `remove_all` and `retain_all` return removed counts, evaluating candidate membership outside registry locks and applying conditional removals. Native tests match Java removeAll/retainAll operations on each view for both tables, including equal-but-distinct owner cases. Full workspace tests, strict Clippy, pinned Maven verify, fmt/diff and comparator/manifest22 pass; fixture SHA-256 fc7119b073dbd6e6da0d1219352f7cc91606ad3df11ff3fc7a8e6eced759ec4c. Java iterator/weak iteration and broader API/source/input audit remain open. Preparing implementation commit.
Updated ADR-0009, API map and Phase6 P6-04 audit for Java removeAll/retainAll membership parity and stable equality coverage. The remaining table-view gap is now iterator removal/weak consistency; generic Java Collection signatures are represented by Rust BTreeSet/owner-slice/key-value-map inputs. Final fixture SHA-256 fc7119b073dbd6e6da0d1219352f7cc91606ad3df11ff3fc7a8e6eced759ec4c; full workspace, strict Clippy, pinned Maven, fmt/diff and comparator/manifest22 pass. Phase6 remains incomplete for these and broader input/source items. Preparing separate docs commit.
Pinned route-table fixture now invokes getOrDefault for present/absent topics and putAll with two route owners on the actual Java ConcurrentMap. All three cases pass. `putAll` is verified against raw getter contents while the route conversion pipeline remains independent. Route fixture SHA-256 34f3d9b5be82c3989f90d1f3d1116ee105c9c6d4346b6a7a5a0a4a8203061f43; offline Maven verify passes. Preparing route-oracle-only commit.
Added Rust route-table integration assertions for actual getOrDefault present/absent and putAll cases. Compile-red confirms TopicRouteTable lacks all three methods (exit101). Java source oracle reports true for both getOrDefault outcomes and the two-entry putAll raw-table write; route fixture SHA-256 34f3d9b5be82c3989f90d1f3d1116ee105c9c6d4346b6a7a5a0a4a8203061f43. Preparing separate red-test commit.
Implemented `TopicRouteTable::get_or_default` and `put_all` against the live raw route map. `put_all` applies a single raw-map update and does not run route conversion or publish derived topics. Java actual table regression passes for present/absent defaults and added raw values; native integration preserves the cached query and confirms derived route topics remain absent. Full workspace tests, strict Clippy, pinned Maven verify, fmt/diff and comparator/manifest22 pass. Route fixture SHA-256 34f3d9b5be82c3989f90d1f3d1116ee105c9c6d4346b6a7a5a0a4a8203061f43. Remaining route-table Map methods/defaults and broader Phase6 source/input audit remain open. Preparing implementation commit.
Adjusted the raw-route helper regression cleanup to remove only `bulk-a`/`bulk-b`, retaining the `topic` mapping for the following no-fetch query assertion. A full-table clear here removed the cached raw topic and correctly caused NotStarted, so the fixture test now isolates putAll values. The focused test, full workspace and lint gates pass. Preparing small test cleanup commit.
FactoryTable iterator-removal and null-remapping update: Java 5.5.1 now directly invokes iterator removal for keySet, values and entrySet, and null-return computeIfAbsent, computeIfPresent, absent compute, and merge removal. Rust live-view remove methods match iterator-removal effects; all48 managerTable outcomes pass at fixture SHA-256 27ef695764fb71aa7bcb707279f4bc4e992f3b8fde61223ff58d3effd977272f. Focused manager-table regression, full workspace tests, exact all-feature Clippy, pinned offline Maven verify, fmt/diff, comparator self-test and manifest22 pass. Docs updated in ADR-0009, API map and requirement audit. Weakly consistent traversal, dynamic owner equality, exact generic overload surface and broad Phase6 source/input audit remain open.
SOCKS Fastjson grammar update: the pinned 5.5.1 constructor and reflected parser oracle adds five rejected forms (unquoted identifier value, hex number, undefined, NaN, new Date) and three accepted forms (duplicate-field last wins, line comment, x-escape). Native parser now matches all33 constructor cases and all parsed-value outcomes; fixture SHA-256 1c3c4a9f023952b5d18b3d503c1441f9d6af70a5ccf397680c758e23b1e8f78c. Red regression failed at Java-rejected 0x2a before the parser fix. Full workspace/all-target tests passed with loopback permission, exact all-feature Clippy, offline pinned Maven verify, fmt/diff, comparator self-test and manifest22 passed. Commits: oracle bc5a10d, native red test 21c9fcb, parser fix 3bf035d. Broader Fastjson grammar and live SOCKS connection behavior remain open; Phase6 remains incomplete.
SOCKS CIDR update: pinned Java `RemotingHelper.ipInCIDR` oracle captures12 host/CIDR results, including Java shift masking and `ipToInt` ignoring extra octet and slash fields. Rust test reproduced a red failure for address `10.20.4.5.99`; native now reads the first four components like the Java helper. Current client-config fixture SHA-256 07e8ca582ea56b813a69d3cbedd6031d93f8b74f6dbec245e6d4d7670a3df3c9. Full workspace/all-target tests with loopback permission, exact all-feature Clippy, offline pinned Maven verify, fmt/diff, comparator self-test and manifest22 pass. Commits: Java oracle 1e88146, red test d77c43c, fix c57c8ce. Full proxy selection, additional parser input and live SOCKS connection behavior remain open; Phase6 remains incomplete.
Java SOCKS proxy-selection oracle `47f3fa0` invokes private `NettyRemotingClient.getProxy` through an actual unstarted Java 5.5.1 runtime for eight hit/miss/default/IPv6/null-route/invalid-CIDR/empty-map cases. Native `proxy_for` matches proxy-address/no-proxy/error results; focused remoting regression passes, no production change was needed. Current fixture SHA-256 46762834bf876a467f64bbb01e19327f765fcbb21e4c110189c1173a0f14cdf3. Test commit 8bf543b. End-to-end Java SOCKS handshake and remaining parser grammar remain open; Phase6 remains incomplete.
SOCKS Fastjson grammar update: the pinned Java 5.5.1 constructor/parser oracle adds four rejected forms (Infinity, -Infinity, unquoted identifier field name, binary 0b10) and three accepted forms (single-quoted field name, +123, leading-zero decimal 0123). Native parser matches all40 `socksConstruction` acceptance and reflected-value outcomes; numeric leading-zero normalization runs outside strings/comments. Oracle/fixture `300ca27`, implementation `0c07502`, fixture SHA-256 `da3b0dcdab5a83db0b4d7c9051009f54f46e614d557439662c24f4d0272ffa2f`. Focused config/core tests, full socket-enabled workspace tests, strict all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify, fmt/diff pass. Broader grammar, end-to-end Java SOCKS connection behavior, weakly consistent table-view traversal, dynamic owner equality and full Phase6 source/API/input audit remain open; P6-V04 remains pending Phase19. Both changes committed separately.
Additional Java SOCKS parser oracle captures nine boundary inputs: Java accepts signed leading-zero integers, leading-zero decimals, negative fractional notation, arrays and objects, preserving object field order when coercing nested `addr` values to String; it rejects octal and signed hexadecimal forms. The 49-case fixture currently hashes `1ab5d96f11e22c865128efdb058bc6baedc8ef628beb1ab968a9bb2c8af689ba`. The existing native differential test is red on reversed object field order (`{"port":1080,"host":"proxy"}` becomes sorted by serde_json). Maven verify correctly reported fixture drift before regeneration; direct pinned Java fixture generation succeeded. Preparing separate oracle commit before ordered-value parser fix.
The parser oracle now includes a nested object string with escaped quote/newline, Unicode and slash. Pinned Java preserves insertion order and emits compact escaping; the ordered native renderer matches this tenth new case. Fixture count is 50 and SHA-256 is `3c7b1c5efbbba26f0fa24ca2fa72971db9631d57463f3f10e841004e60b27c65`; focused native parsed-value differential passes. This fixture-only extension is committed separately before full implementation gates.
Ordered SOCKS value fix committed `85bb68d`: replaced private serde_json map coercion with a Deserialize visitor retaining object insertion order and a compact escaped JSON renderer, matching Java Fastjson's `addr` string conversion. Focused remoting config tests (9), core SOCKS construction (1), full socket-enabled workspace suite, strict all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (50 cases, manifest22), comparator self-test, fmt and diff pass. The original 49-case mismatch was reproduced before the change. Broader parser grammar, live Java SOCKS handshake, weak table traversal, mutable owner equality and final bidirectional Phase6 audit remain open; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.
ConcurrentMap traversal audit: Oracle Java SE 8 `ConcurrentHashMap` docs guarantee iteration entries present at construction, permit but do not require later changes, and prohibit fail-fast exceptions. Existing detached snapshots at traversal start provide one permitted result while retained handles preserve live view reads/writes; iterator-removal effects already map to explicit remove methods. Updated ADR-0009/0010, route/API maps and requirement audit with this source-backed ownership mapping. Dynamic owner equality, mutable route DTO aliasing and broader API/input reconciliation remain open. Phase6 remains PARTIAL; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
Dynamic owner equality oracle: extended the pinned Java 5.5.1 producer/consumer table fixture with mutable equals keys. The oracle captures containsValue before and after mutating either owner, plus conditional replace against a stale and current expected key. Fixture SHA-256 `6bfe7bb6ce6bd07bb75fb8a817524603dbfbc5f83e0c9ac7db6808f48cb4bb64`; native regression and implementation are still pending. Broader Phase6 reconciliation remains open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
Dynamic equality red regression: native `conditional_registry_mutations_match_java_custom_value_equality` now covers mutable consumer equality keys and checks all five pinned oracle outcomes. Focused test compiles and fails as expected: cached insertion keys make both `dynamicContainsAfterStoredMutation`, `dynamicContainsAfterBothMutations`, and `dynamicReplaceMatchesCurrentEquality` false where Java returns true. Regression test commit is separate from the upcoming production fix.
Dynamic equality test setup correction: registry table values are weakly held, so the first test version failed to retain the mutable owners and accidentally observed expired mappings. The test now holds producer/consumer Arcs across assertions. Under the live-owner contract, the focused parity test passes with the uncommitted current-key comparison change; the prior failure did not demonstrate the cache mismatch and is superseded by this corrected test.
Dynamic Java owner equality implementation: removed equality keys cached at registration/insertion. `contains_value`, entry membership, and `_if_equal` replace/remove now sample each live owner's key outside registry locks; conditional writes compare a detached strong owner and commit through identity-conditional mutation with retries. The corrected regression fails against the committed cached-key implementation and passes with this change. Full workspace tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, pinned offline Maven verify (73 config cases and manifest22), differential comparator, fmt and diff checks pass. Fixture SHA-256 `6bfe7bb6ce6bd07bb75fb8a817524603dbfbc5f83e0c9ac7db6808f48cb4bb64`. Preparing the implementation commit and current audit updates; broad Phase 6 source/input reconciliation remains open.
Registry equality audit update: ADR-0009, the Phase 6 API/config map, runtime inventory and requirement audit now record comparison-time mutable-key behavior, the pinned Java cases, and passing regression/gates. P6-04 no longer lists mutable equality as open; broad Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remains incomplete, and P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
Route DTO alias oracle: pinned Java 5.5.1 `getTopicRouteTable()` stores the exact mutable `TopicRouteData` passed to `put`; source and table getter references observe each other's setters. Added actual unstarted-runtime fixture outcomes for both directions, all true at route-fixture SHA-256 `27d8e568e0e5042aa891cdd08af94b7ffd28667e1dd02d3df5d94d7650646e65`. The current Rust `Arc<TopicRouteData>` API cannot mutate a shared DTO; the native adaptation remains pending. Broader Phase 6 reconciliation and P6-V04 remain open.
Route alias red regression: added `raw_topic_table_values_preserve_mutable_java_aliases`, which requires a shared route-data handle with snapshot/write access and compares both Java mutation directions to the pinned fixture. Focused test fails at compile time because `TopicRouteDataHandle`, `snapshot`, and `with_mut` are absent from the current raw table API. Preparing a separate implementation commit; route alias semantics remain open.
Route DTO alias implementation: `TopicRouteDataHandle` now wraps `Arc<RwLock<TopicRouteData>>`; raw table and runtime cached-route getters preserve shared object identity, while `snapshot()` returns a DTO copy and `with_mut()` updates all aliases. Route lookup snapshots DTOs before route-cache writes to avoid holding value locks with cache locks. Converted `TopicSnapshot` values remain immutable copies. Commits: Java oracle `c085d03`, red regression `82430b5`, implementation `03e3925`, strict-Clippy return cleanup `3f3e24e`. Fixture SHA-256 `27d8e568e0e5042aa891cdd08af94b7ffd28667e1dd02d3df5d94d7650646e65`. Core crate tests (82 unit tests plus all core integration targets), full `cargo test --workspace --all-targets --locked`, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator self-test, manifest validation22, fmt and diff checks pass. Mutable route alias gap is closed for the invoked behaviors; broader Phase 6 source/input reconciliation remains open and P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
SOCKS numeric/scalar oracle: actual Java 5.5.1 runtime cases expand `socksConstruction` from 50 to 61 and cover exponent formatting, signed zero, exact high-precision decimal text, overflow/underflow and escaped Unicode keys/values. The native differential was red at `-0.0`; numeric-token preservation now matches all Java reflected proxy-map values, including `1e309` → `Infinity` and `1e-1000` → `0.0`. Fixture SHA-256 `36330978d061dd3ce2eedac8926b366da5233822929beea3c3b4adab2bf1db38`. Full workspace/all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, pinned offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator/manifest22, fmt and diff pass. Oracle commit `457d16b`; native parser commit `37af420`. Additional Fastjson grammar, end-to-end Java SOCKS connection and full Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.
SOCKS numeric threshold follow-up: Java 5.5.1 exponent output follows scientific thresholds (`1e-4` → `1.0E-4`, `1e-7` → `1.0E-7`, `1e7` → `1.0E7`), accepts signed leading-dot forms but rejects unsigned `.5e-3`, preserves decimal scale `1.2300`, and returns `-Infinity` for `-1e309`. Added actual Java oracle cases and native token/formatter parity; the 73-case differential passes. Fixture SHA-256 `a1054ec9af61312d25037da4470d17629babee026d4e6da6371cb9555b81e175`. Workspace/all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator/manifest22, fmt and diff pass. Oracle commit `09d0878`; parser commit `6c4d59b`. Other Fastjson inputs, end-to-end SOCKS connection and full Phase 6 audit remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
BrokerData equality audit: six actual pinned Java 5.5.1 cases prove `equals` compares only brokerName and brokerAddrs, ignoring cluster, zoneName and enableActingMaster. Native `BrokerData::PartialEq` now matches the Java DTO, including null-map versus empty-map and null address values; `TopicRouteData` equality inherits it. The native regression failed on a metadata-only difference before the fix. Route fixture SHA-256 `b2c35d8c5d61e36fa9244641b323aaa0a28395187bc3983be6cb8daa10830131`. Full workspace/all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator/manifest22, fmt and diff pass. Commits: Java oracle `04848b0`, native red test `dcfa7da`, implementation `2c6a476`. Other route DTO methods/input combinations and full Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
BrokerData comparison audit: six actual Java 5.5.1 `compareTo` pairs capture raw UTF-16 code-unit differences, prefix-length results, equal names and null-name exceptions; three direct `TopicRouteData.topicRouteDataChanged` cases capture null-name broker sorting, including the single-entry no-comparison case. The native API regression was compile-red before `BrokerData::java_compare_to`; the route-change regression then failed because Rust sorted null names instead of returning an error. Rust now uses Java comparison for route broker sorting and reports the observed multi-entry null-name failure as `InvalidRoute`. Final route fixture SHA-256 `b3197eb0f792d120fb6923cb781f6f18623a598b0c139e3b5668b53cc49a4001`. Commits: direct Java comparison oracle `9dfaa53`, red API regression `ac3b604`, comparison method `533600a`, route-change oracle `13248bf`, red route regression `cec1821`, sort correction `c7b32bc`. Full workspace/all-target tests (core83), strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator self-test, manifest validation22, fmt and diff pass. Remaining DTO methods, input families and full Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation are still open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
BrokerData hashCode audit: three actual pinned Java values cover null fields, a supplementary Unicode name, and address maps containing signed Long keys plus null and supplementary Unicode values. The native `java_hash_code` regression failed to compile before the method, then matched all three exact hash integers using Java Map, Long and UTF-16 String rules. Final route fixture SHA-256 `66c4e668072c05c0b6b5a88460e6ed9a8099d86392d687af9d7579a2bd65a3a8`. Commits: Java oracle `f0607f9`, native red test `20cff94`, implementation `e6a3389`. Full workspace/all-target tests (core83), strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator self-test, manifest validation22, fmt and diff pass. `BrokerData.toString`, setter/getter surfaces, other DTO/input families and whole Phase 6 reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
QueueData method audit: five actual Java cases capture all-field equals, exact hashCode/toString, raw UTF-16 compareTo, and null-name NPE. The direct Rust method regression was compile-red before the three DTO methods. The six-case `topicRouteDataChanged` oracle now includes QueueData null-name and reordering cases; temporarily restoring the previous optional-name sort made the core regression fail, and the Java comparator/error handling passes all cases. Final route fixture SHA-256 `6ebf2aa430d170e84b3eae36baffb359a4a7e8e148acaca4ecb27e1bb7c61c8e`. Commits: Java method oracle `329b0f9`, red test `b04b2d9`, QueueData route-sort oracle `1df78b5`, implementation `f6add71`. Full workspace/all-target tests (core83), strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator self-test, manifest validation22, fmt and diff pass. Remaining DTO methods and input combinations, full Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation, and P6-V04 remain open.
TopicQueueMappingInfo method audit: four actual Java pairs cover equals/hashCode/toString for default fields, explicit null versus empty currIdMap, populated IDs and changed dirty state. The native regression failed to compile before `java_hash_code/java_to_string`, then matches exact hash values and captured strings; Rust emits currIdMap entries by deterministic key order because Java ConcurrentHashMap order is unspecified. Final route fixture SHA-256 `dae0e00eaa1d698f00b3f6fe1a9fae1905a2b273bd70369a0b359a09ef926299`. Commits: Java oracle `18f8565`, native red test `af642aa`, implementation `38ec7a8`. Full workspace/all-target tests (core83), strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator self-test, manifest validation22, fmt and diff pass. Other DTO methods/input combinations and Phase 6 reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
TopicRouteData equality/hash audit: four actual Java pairs cover default construction, explicit null versus empty collections, metadata-only nested BrokerData changes and a queue difference. Derived Rust equality matches; the native `java_hash_code` regression was compile-red before its implementation and now matches all four Java hashes, including nested list, map and DTO hash rules. Final route fixture SHA-256 `3dc47fdc1e774357747853f4dfe270f4f1684a8a302d5502f905109a35b76891`. Commits: Java oracle `f9f6450`, native red test `c7d8c01`, implementation `21cc626`. Full workspace/all-target tests (core83), strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator self-test, manifest validation22, fmt and diff pass. TopicRouteData.toString and nullable collection elements, other DTO/input families and full Phase 6 reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
Route DTO toString audit: pinned Java 5.5.1 now emits two BrokerData and three TopicRouteData text cases, covering default/null values, a null address value, explicit null route collections, and populated nested queue/broker/filter/mapping DTOs. Native red regressions were compile-failing before `BrokerData::java_to_string` and `TopicRouteData::java_to_string`; both methods now match actual Java text, with deterministic Rust map-key order where Java HashMap iteration is unspecified. Commits: Java oracle `07e62e8`, native regression `449e97e`, implementation `1d6f799`. Route fixture SHA-256 `d26481b826d4323e5e1f017108de2772051b0caf968257642a101a4f48537fef`. Full cargo workspace/all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator self-test, manifest validation22, fmt and diff pass. Nullable nested collection elements and the wider source/API/input reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
Nullable nested route and public change-method audit: actual Java fixtures now cover null QueueData/BrokerData elements, null filter-list and mapping values, all four TopicRouteData nested collections, and 11 `topicRouteDataChanged` outcomes including `old == null` and sort-time NPEs. Rust preserves those nullable values, rejects invalid queue/broker/static-mapping entries before publishing a refreshed route, retains null filter lists, and routes cache comparison through `TopicRouteData::java_topic_route_data_changed`. Added direct protocol and core regressions; both focused tests pass. Route fixture SHA-256 `fc8277fe53b84a624d6af12501993cb09038a447b9401348f34b7dbdf12e86e3`. Commits: null/method Java oracle and red regressions `477aa48` through `6207d19`; route sort error detail correction `114178e`. Updated route/API/requirement audits. Java TopicRouteData copy/clone aliasing and broad Phase 6 source/API/input reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
Route copy-constructor mapping: existing Java `nullableRouteCollections` oracle outcomes now drive a direct `java_copy_constructed` regression. The regression was commit `14057e3`, initially compile-red for the missing method; implementation `e1191be` normalizes null queue/broker/filter collections, preserves nullable mapping table, and is reused by route publication and `topicRouteDataChanged`. Focused protocol/core tests pass. Full workspace/all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), differential self-test, manifest22, fmt and diff checks pass. Route fixture SHA-256 remains `fc8277fe53b84a624d6af12501993cb09038a447b9401348f34b7dbdf12e86e3`. Direct Java shallow/deep clone helper aliasing and remaining source/API/input reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
BrokerData address selection audit: pinned Java 5.5.1 `BrokerData.selectBrokerAddr` was missing from the native DTO API. Java oracle commit `33ba5de` adds seven actual cases for master-first selection, no-master random values, null master/address values, null-map NPE and empty-map IAE; fixture SHA-256 `a006476a1eceef2ecf6c45dd82fddb8c028eb07d454cc35cf436545f4fcda0e9`. Native red regression `c90be31` failed to compile before the method. Implementation `a16902f` adds `BrokerData::java_select_broker_addr` with typed error outcomes and a private deterministic selector used to test every fallback value. Full workspace/all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), differential self-test, manifest22, fmt and diff checks pass. Direct TopicRouteData shallow/deep clone alias semantics and broad source/API/input reconciliation remain open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
BrokerData selection documentation: updated route API, source-method and requirement audits with `selectBrokerAddr`, its seven invoked inputs and current fixture digest. Full workspace/all-target tests, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, offline Java verify, comparator self-test/manifest22, fmt and diff all pass. Public route clone-helper aliases and remaining source/API/input reconciliation are still open; P6-V04 remains assigned to Phase 19.
TopicRouteData clone API audit: Java 5.5.1 copy/clone/deep-clone oracle covers eight cases for null root collections, null nested QueueData/BrokerData/filter/mapping values, valid nested route data, clone output values, and shallow/deep element identity. Fixture SHA-256 `08038bfb606aaa057869cb3e41256a410ec03d8c4f85003aa32055be69ea21a2`. Oracle commits `dca2e47`/`2987bf5`; regression `78a598e` failed to compile before `clone_topic_route_data` and `deep_clone_topic_route_data`; implementation `76d6f74` passes all eight value/error cases. Rust returns owned nested values; `TopicRouteDataHandle` continues to represent live raw-table identity. Full workspace/all-target tests, strict Clippy, offline Maven verify (route25/config73/manifest22), comparator self-test, manifest22, fmt and diff pass. Broad Phase 6 API/input reconciliation remains open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
Route DTO reverse-method inventory: pinned `javap` confirms the public constructors/accessors alongside `BrokerData.selectBrokerAddr`, comparison/equality/hash/text methods, `TopicRouteData.topicRouteDataChanged`, and copy/clone helpers. The API map now explicitly maps no-arg constructors to `Default`, copy/default variants to Rust owned copies, Java getters/setters to public DTO fields, and inherited `toJson` to serde encoding. The only documented ownership difference is Java's nested alias behavior for shallow clone; raw runtime table aliases remain shared handles. Current fixture `08038bfb606aaa057869cb3e41256a410ec03d8c4f85003aa32055be69ea21a2`; full workspace, strict Clippy, Maven verify, comparator/manifest22, fmt and diff pass. Broader whole-phase source/input reconciliation remains open; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
